{offset100}{ia8}{arial}



{offset205}{arialbld}Tyron Spirex{arial}

Strategic Command of Pristan{offset0}







My TSUNAMI plan is working marvellously. 

However {name}, you almost ruined everything at Bikin. My tanks landed under sustained fire while your navy was circling around in the water, safely out of the Parano coastal artillery's range. In the future make sure to be there when I need you.{pause}

Our next candidate for extreme surfing is named {arialbld}Yorik{arial}. He's presently taking his winter holidays at {arialbld}Vostok{arial}. He is armed to the teeth.{pause}


Yorik is from the Kozak clan, a real brute, he's known by a little nickname: "The Flying Turkey". His parents raised chickens in Tcherkassian, already as a child he helped to scald the birds.{pause}

{ia17}{offset110}When he was 15 the family farm was pillaged by the Kozak army passing by. Captivated by such savagery he joined the army, but since he couldn't stay on a horse, he tried his hand as a bomber in the nascent Kozak air force. From there he worked miracles. In those times bombs were thrown by hand from the cockpit. When asked about this ability he responded: "It's like flinging a chicken into a pot of boiling water from the roof of the henhouse...{offset0}{pause}


I dare not imagine the fate of the Nikonese population at the mercy of such a sadist.{pause}

Vostok has recently received an important fleet of heavy bombers. You can be sure they will be disturbing our sleep...{pause}

The Normo Research Centre for Defense, always worried about our comfort, has sent us a new system to strike back against these nocturnal nuisances. It's called RADAR, and its only purpose is to detect the position of approaching enemy bombers. So when the sirens go off, our Kormoran pilots can intercept the Turkey's airplanes BEFORE they try to devastate my Nikonese garden. 



{offset150}{arialbld}Tyron Spirex{arial}

Ingenious Chief of Operation TSUNAMI




